 HISTORY                                                          8160 1451
 -------                                                          8160 1451
    This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction       8160 1451
    Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. 8160 1451
    The thermal scattering law data for Carbon in Uranium Carbide 8160 1451
    was developed using ab initio lattice dynamics (AILD)[1,2].   8160 1451
    Ten temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law  8160 1451
    Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to    8160 1451
    produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data for Carbon in UC [3]. MAT=8160  8160 1451
    and ZA=8260 are used for C (10% enriched U)  in UC. Elemental 8160 1451
    AWR and cross sections were computed from ENDF/B-VIII.0 MF=3  8160 1451
    MT=2 nuclide evaluations [4] at 1e-5eV with C-12 updated to   8160 1451
    reflect a mass of exactly 12 amu.                             8160 1451
